{"id": "EUVD-2026-93211", "enisaUuid": "4588a903-a15b-3cba-971c-85eb22fde9bc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: PPC: Book3S HV: fix use-after-free in kvmhv_emulate_tlbie_all_lpid()\n\nkvmhv_emulate_tlbie_all_lpid() iterates the nested-guest IDR and drops\nmmu_lock before calling kvmhv_emulate_tlbie_lpid(), but does not hold a\nreference on the kvm_nested_guest pointer obtained from the IDR.  A\nconcurrent vCPU issuing a single-LPID tlbie (is=2, ric=2) can race\nthrough kvmhv_flush_nested() -> kvmhv_remove_nested() -> idr_remove /\n--refcnt -> kvmhv_release_nested() -> kfree(gp) in that window, leaving\nthe iterating vCPU with a dangling pointer.  The subsequent\nmutex_lock(&gp->tlb_lock) and accesses to gp->shadow_pgtable,\ngp->shadow_lpid and gp->l1_host all touch freed memory.  The free path\nis fully L1-controlled.\n\nFix this by incrementing gp->refcnt inside the loop before dropping\nmmu_lock, mirroring what kvmhv_get_nested() does, and releasing the\nreference with kvmhv_put_nested() after the per-guest work completes.\nThis is the same get/put discipline already used at every other\ncall site that drops mmu_lock while holding a nested-guest pointer.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:54", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4d8f7b1f586375df8bce23a0909566ad5e852259", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e37fba1ba69385cff2d0e60b371ee19e7d1852d1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/24b634852413229bb8340d908b115c3365f3a247", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fbf69b7d0555ee83c871f58750770f74b7179ad1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ec2d7a52b3996ae81131617b4afc0af31583c1b4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51938dfa8a51a4f85328413fca9b6e21f9d2d088"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f6vc-5ch2-5vxm", "CVE-2026-98283"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b89f1fa-ef4a-3706-babe-33fbce34824e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3b6b4661527e821ffbe3db83952fdb1e6e47c49 <fbf69b7d0555ee83c871f58750770f74b7179ad1"}, {"id": "6ad59cd6-cbdc-3f97-83f9-462cdb84fd4e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "7310d310-a0de-3799-984e-47712afa918c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3b6b4661527e821ffbe3db83952fdb1e6e47c49 <4d8f7b1f586375df8bce23a0909566ad5e852259"}, {"id": "7c76fc8a-1904-3559-be6b-765cf7de561d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "7cd21de1-dfc5-3872-aae8-2cceebbc4e9e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "8f998379-1726-3e07-98d6-07dcff60412e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.20"}, {"id": "aa0463bb-2d05-3ba0-8b8e-b9488db87373", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b662f338-19e4-3bd1-97dc-ff605b24bf54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "c1b44adb-b080-399a-ba62-c147f456ccb4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3b6b4661527e821ffbe3db83952fdb1e6e47c49 <51938dfa8a51a4f85328413fca9b6e21f9d2d088"}, {"id": "c1f29ee4-a38b-30ea-b03c-77fbbc60e620", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3b6b4661527e821ffbe3db83952fdb1e6e47c49 <24b634852413229bb8340d908b115c3365f3a247"}, {"id": "c8803383-3f5c-3c96-a328-773d85bbdac1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3b6b4661527e821ffbe3db83952fdb1e6e47c49 <e37fba1ba69385cff2d0e60b371ee19e7d1852d1"}, {"id": "caf7665c-0605-3075-ae6c-fc66aff4e96a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {